# windowlight signal map: which behaviour of the window each signal drives.
#
# This copy is built into windowlight. To change it, copy it to ~/.config/windowlight/signals.map
# (or point $WINDOWLIGHT_SIGNAL_MAP at a file); that file reloads on save.
#
#   signal-pattern   behaviour   [from..to]
#
# A pattern is a signal name, with * matching anything. A signal can appear on several lines, and several
# signals can drive one behaviour (the strongest wins). from..to stretches part of a signal's level over the
# whole behaviour: `disk frost 0.8..1` frosts the glass only once the disk is past 80% full.
#
# Behaviours, each driven by a signal's level (0..1) and reacting when it turns done or alert:
#   birds       one bird per signal: circles outside while busy, pecks at the glass while waiting,
#               sits on the sill when done, flies off on alert or when it goes quiet
#   wind        the plant and curtain sway harder; a gust on done or alert
#   dust        more dust drifting in the light shaft
#   frost       frost creeps in from the frame, any season
#   haze        the light softens and spreads
#   rain        drops on the glass
#   shade       a cloud dims the sun
#   suncatcher  the crystal hangs in the window and turns faster; a spin on done or alert
#   passing     birds (by day) or headlights (by night) go past on done, alert, or a jump past 75%
#   cat         the cat walks along the sill on done, alert, or a jump past 75%
#
# The default adapters (adapters/herdr and adapters/system) write the signals below.

herdr-*   birds
cpu       wind
net       dust
disk      frost   0.8..1
